<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sheth et al. (2012) Science distal Hoxa13/Hoxd11-13 + Gli3 dose modulation of Turing digit wavelength on a fan-shaped embryonic autopod, with Pass 3 AER-FGF8 mitogenic outgrowth on a deforming Lagrangian mesh — Code-to-model traceability: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-72) now maps the growing-domain equations term by term to Crampin et al. (1999), Boehm et al. (2010) and Summerbell (1974) and lists all five Lean theorems; the solver docstring (L527-551) restates the ALE equations, the zone kinetics and the Lean cross-references; the math KG YAML registers Laws 4-5 with lean_code, code_locus and source citations. Deductions: the g_u closure (L183) remains uncited; GROWTH_* constants (L431-445) carry comments but no source; the choice of the sub-Turing wrist gate f_u = 1.5 / g_u = 1500 (L601-603) is traced only to the Pass 2 negative control (-7)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py L179–L183: k_c(H) = 14 - 9H and the g_u closure have no equation-level citation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L179-L183>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sheth et al. (2012) Science distal Hoxa13/Hoxd11-13 + Gli3 dose modulation of Turing digit wavelength on a fan-shaped embryonic autopod, with Pass 3 AER-FGF8 mitogenic outgrowth on a deforming Lagrangian mesh — Model fidelity to source: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Retains the exact Sheth et al. (2012) dispersion and cubic PDE (L160-243, L248-328) and adds the growing-domain reaction-diffusion equations in the Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999) form with every term present: AER-FGF8 mitogen field and kinematic dilation (L587), radial velocity from mass conservation (L589-591), ALE advection relative to the mesh (L614-622), dilution -g u / -g v folded into the implicit linear operator (L607-610), physical-metric angular modes k_m = pi m / (Theta r(t)) (L606), backward-Euler polar radial diffusion (L631-643), rim outgrowth and Lagrangian tracers (L646-647); the mathematics is backed by Lean Theorems 4-5 (0 sorrys). Deductions: growth is kinematic with no constitutive law or stress balance, so \"tissue mechanics\" is only partially met (-3); stripe orientation is imposed by eps_r = 0.05 diffusion anisotropy (L631) instead of the Fgf/Wnt gradient of Raspopovic et al. (-2); g_u(H) (L183) and k_c(H) = 14 - 9H (L179) are closure ansaetze not taken from the paper's supplement (-2); the 1D arc and fixed fan seed the target mode (L284, L375-376), which the growing fan shows matters (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py L284–L284: 1D arc seeds -0.08 cos(n_target s): the Pass 2 'exact integer mode lock' is partly an initial-condition artefact (growing fan without seeding gives 3.5 for WT) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L284-L284>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sheth et al. (2012) Science distal Hoxa13/Hoxd11-13 + Gli3 dose modulation of Turing digit wavelength on a fan-shaped embryonic autopod, with Pass 3 AER-FGF8 mitogenic outgrowth on a deforming Lagrangian mesh — Morphometric validation: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` now returns 15 reference-backed measurements (L1281-1470): the 8 Pass 2 metrics plus the calibrated WT arc (2500.0 vs 2500 um), growing-fan WT and null wavelength counts (3.5 vs 5.0; 13.0 vs 13.6), the growing-fan allelic Pearson r vs k_c(H), the width-law Pearson r over 18 runs (0.996, slope 0.90), the AER-ablation arc fraction (0.546) and the dilution margin sigma_max - g_rim (2.54). Deductions: the WT growing-fan count misses its reference by 30 % and is explained rather than resolved (-4); several Pass 3 references are qualitative or model-internal (Summerbell ordering with reference 1.0 = intact control, Crampin threshold 0.0, law r = 1.0) rather than measured specimen values (-4); Sheth et al.'s Fig. 2G digit-period / width data are still not digitised into the dataset (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py L1364–L1376: AER-ablation measurement uses the intact control (1.0) as reference: Summerbell (1974) stage-vs-truncation values are not vendored <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L1364-L1376>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-aer-ablation-at-t-0-6-wt-autopod-arc-fraction-l-abl-l-intact>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-aer-grown-allelic-series-n-grow-vs-k-c-h-pearson-r-h-1-7-9-5-9-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-aer-grown-triple-null-rim-digit-wavelength-count-n-grow-h-0-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-aer-grown-wt-autopod-final-arc-width-l-t-at-calibrated-g-max>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-aer-grown-wt-rim-digit-wavelength-count-n-grow-h-1-0-vs-quasi-static-l-lambda>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-allelic-series-inverse-wavelength-l-lambda-h-vs-pde-digit-count-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-digit-number-width-wavelength-law-n-grow-vs-l-t-lambda-h-over-g-max-sweep-aer-ablations-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-equal-diffusion-du-dv-and-sub-turing-fu-1-5-negative-control-amplitude>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-gli3-mutant-autopod-pde-digit-count-n-h-0-78>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-growth-dilution-turing-margin-sigma-max-g-rim-during-aer-outgrowth>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-hoxa13-hoxd11-13-gli3-triple-null-pde-digit-count-n-h-0-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-hoxd11-13-gli3-double-mutant-pde-digit-count-n-h-0-56>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-segmented-hexadactylous-autopod-radiograph-digit-ray-count-spacing-cv>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-wt-pentadactyl-autopod-pde-digit-count-n-h-1-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-measurement-wt-to-triple-null-turing-stripe-wavelength-ratio-lambda-wt-lambda-null>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sheth et al. (2012) Science distal Hoxa13/Hoxd11-13 + Gli3 dose modulation of Turing digit wavelength on a fan-shaped embryonic autopod, with Pass 3 AER-FGF8 mitogenic outgrowth on a deforming Lagrangian mesh — MorphoEval overall 91.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) post-remediation evaluation of `2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py` (overall weighted score: 91.3 / 100, -0.8 from 92.1 in Pass 2). The single open Pass 2 item is closed as an honest reduced version: the 2D polar fan Turing solver is now coupled to a deforming Lagrangian mesh whose distal rim grows under an AER-FGF8 mitogen field with prescribed kinematic dilation, solved in the Crampin-Gaffney-Maini ALE form (dilution, mesh-relative advection, deformed polar metric, backward-Euler radial diffusion). The growing fan reproduces monotone digit addition with Hox loss (N_grow = 3.5, 5.5, 7.5, 13.0 for H = 1, 7/9, 5/9, 0), monotone digit number with AER-driven width over a g_max sweep (r = 0.996 against N = L/lambda, slope 0.90), the Summerbell AER-ablation ordering (L = 1365, 1667, 1990, 2500 um), and the growth-dilution threshold sigma_max - g_rim = 2.54 > 0 (Lean Theorem 5). The remediation also exposed that the Pass 2 solvers seed their target mode and that the WT growing fan under-counts digits (3.5 vs 5) through a growth-induced wavelength lag; model-fidelity, specimen-match and morphometric-validation are scored down accordingly while traceability and reproducibility rise. Overall 91.3/100 (faithfulness 90.3, reproducibility 93.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 58b898c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/hox_turing_polydactyly_comparison.png: rendered output of 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py at 58b898c, image/png, 1085114 B, 2193×1981 px, artifact_sha256 4f0e23e35e7cb8c99037a2861ab479bf20313159bb3b61db076535db0ba71572 (sha256 4f0e23e35e7cb8c99037a2861ab479bf20313159bb3b61db076535db0ba71572), spec_fingerprint df2380b6b9d39cc7343d21970d756072ccaee92ea4d1cd0e08f469c328909c2c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: df2380b6b9d39cc7343d21970d756072ccaee92ea4d1cd0e08f469c328909c2c; artifact_sha256: 4f0e23e35e7cb8c99037a2861ab479bf20313159bb3b61db076535db0ba71572; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/hox_turing_polydactyly_reference.json=06c60968ccdce3a7..., datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/pass3_aer_growth_reference.json=311a1e81311eabab..., datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/scout_manifest.json=c0608869f6d213a4..., datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/vertebrate_autopod_digits_specimen.jpg=995e43a2a0cf7815...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-hox-turing-polydactyly-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Sheth et al. (2012): progressive loss of distal Hox (Hoxa13, Hoxd11-13) in a Gli3-null background shrinks the digit period (wavelength) of a Turing-type mechanism, raising digit number from 5 to ~14 at roughly constant autopod width (Figs. 1-3) | Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999): on a growing domain the reaction-diffusion equations acquire an advection term and a dilution term -(div v) u; patterns lag the fixed-domain wavelength and transition by peak insertion / frequency doubling | Boehm et al. (2010): limb bud proliferation is distally biased but a proliferation gradient alone is insufficient to explain bud shape | Summerbell (1974): AER excision arrests distal outgrowth; the earlier the excision the more proximal the truncation; reconstructed_in_script: Sheth et al. (2012) linear dispersion, k_c(H) and the cubic-saturated two-component PDE on a 1D Neumann arc and a 2D fixed-width polar fan (Pass 2), plus the Pass 3 AER-FGF8 kinematic growing fan in ALE form with dilution, mesh-relative advection, physical-metric angular modes, backward-Euler radial diffusion, Lagrangian tracers, AER regression and ablation, a g_max sweep and the quasi-static digit-number/width law; 6-genotype allelic series; dual negative controls; radiograph digit-ray segmentation; 5 Lean 4 theorems; transfer_boundary: Growth is kinematic: g(r,t) is prescribed by the mitogen field and div v = g; no elastic/viscous constitutive law, stress balance or oriented cell behaviour is solved (Boehm et al. 2010 show these matter for shape) | Digit-ray (stripe) orientation is imposed by PD/AP diffusion anisotropy D_r = 0.05 D rather than derived from the Fgf/Wnt proximodistal modulation of Raspopovic et al. (2014) | k_c(H) = 14 - 9H and g_u(H) = 200 f_u + 25 k_c^4 - 4.5|tr J_kc| are closure ansaetze that interpolate the allelic series and pin sigma_max ~ 4.5; they are not fitted to Sheth et al.'s supplementary parameter values | The 1D arc and fixed-width fan solvers seed the target cosine mode (-0.08 cos(n_target s)); only the Pass 3 growing fan evolves from seeded noise alone, and it shows a growth-induced wavelength lag (N_grow = 3.5 WT, 13.0 null vs law 5 / 14); does_not_claim: 3D limb bud geometry, cell-level mechanics, Sox9/Bmp/Wnt three-node kinetics, quantitative reproduction of Sheth et al.'s Fig. 2G digit-period measurements (not vendored), or hour-calibrated developmental time." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py:1364-1376 — the AER-ablation measurement is referenced only to the intact control (1.0) with Summerbell (1974) cited qualitatively; digitise Summerbell's stage-vs-truncation table so the ablation series has quantitative reference values.",
        "remediation needed: 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py:179-183 — k_c(H) = 14 - 9H and g_u(H) = 200 f_u + 25 k_c^4 - 4.5 |tr J_kc| are closure ansaetze that pin sigma_max ~ 4.5; digitise Sheth et al.'s supplementary parameter table and Fig. 2G digit-period vs autopod-width measurements into datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/ and fit H -> k_c and the dispersion against them.",
        "remediation needed: 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py:284 and 375-376 — the 1D arc and the fixed-width fan seed the target cosine mode (-0.08 cos(n_target s), -0.10 cos(k_c s)), so the Pass 2 \"exact integer mode lock\" [5, 7, 8, 9, 11, 14] and the 2 -> 5 / 2 -> 14 fan counts are partly initial-condition artefacts (the noise-only growing fan gives 3.5 WT / 13.0 null). Report noise-only counts for all solvers (with an ensemble over seeds) and move the seeded runs to an explicitly labelled 'mode-locked' control.",
        "remediation needed: 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py:431-445 — GROWTH_R0 = 1.6, GROWTH_L_F = 0.5, GROWTH_T_AER_OFF = 2.4 and GROWTH_T_TOTAL = 5.0 are unsourced modelling choices in model time; anchor them to Boehm et al. (2010) limb-bud dimensions / proliferation rates and convert model time to hours (E10.5-E12.5), so sigma_max and g_rim become comparable with measured cell-cycle times.",
        "remediation needed: 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py:512-703 and 631 — growth is kinematic (prescribed dilation, div v = g) and digit-ray orientation is imposed by eps_r = 0.05 radial/angular diffusion anisotropy. Replace with a mechanical tissue model (e.g. Stokes/viscous or Morishita-Iwasa elastic growth with an FGF8-driven volumetric source and stress-dependent anisotropy) and derive stripe orientation from a Raspopovic et al. (2014) Fgf/Wnt proximodistal modulation of the kinetics instead of the anisotropy.",
        "remediation needed: 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py:706-730 and 1147-1179 — the width-law slope 0.90 (Panel L) mixes growth-rate and final-width effects because the g_max sweep changes both; add a sweep at fixed final L (vary g_max and T jointly) to isolate the Crampin growth lag and test peak insertion explicitly." ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.13e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sheth et al. (2012) Science distal Hoxa13/Hoxd11-13 + Gli3 dose modulation of Turing digit wavelength on a fan-shaped embryonic autopod, with Pass 3 AER-FGF8 mitogenic outgrowth on a deforming Lagrangian mesh — Parameter expressivity: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Two new, biologically meaningful control axes are exercised and behave monotonically: AER mitogenic strength g_max (5 values x 2 genotypes, L706-730; L(T) 1410 -> 2947 um and N_grow 2.0 -> 4.5 WT, 7.5 -> 15.0 null) and AER ablation time (L733-752; L = 1365, 1667, 1990, 2500 um with N_grow non-decreasing), on top of the Pass 2 Hox dose, diffusivities and kinetic couplings; the growing fan allelic series is strictly monotone in H (self-test check 10, L1536-1542) and the CLI exposes --g-max, --aer-ablation-time and --growth-only (L1591-1593). Deductions: l_F, eps_r, noise_amp, t_aer_off are fixed constants, not swept (-3); N_grow is quantised to half-wavelengths so small parameter changes are invisible (-2); the growth lag means g_max does not map onto the law line (slope 0.90) (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py L431–L445: GROWTH_* constants (l_F, eps_r, noise_amp, t_aer_off, R0) are fixed and not swept <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L431-L445>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sheth et al. (2012) Science distal Hoxa13/Hoxd11-13 + Gli3 dose modulation of Turing digit wavelength on a fan-shaped embryonic autopod, with Pass 3 AER-FGF8 mitogenic outgrowth on a deforming Lagrangian mesh — Reproducibility package: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`--self-test` runs 14 deterministic checks in ~25 s (L1476-1580), including bitwise two-run determinism for both the 1D arc and the growing fan with its seeded persistent noise (L1566-1569), SHA-256 verification of 5 inputs, calibration of the 2500 um arc, tracer/rim consistency, monotone sweeps and the ablation ordering; the default render completes in ~66 s and regenerates the PNG, the growth-mesh PNG and the GIF; a memo cache (L447, L555-556, L702) avoids recomputing identical growth runs across render/measure/self-test. Deductions: no slot-level requirements lock (the audit records the venv versions) (-3); determinism of the persistent-noise stream depends on numpy's Generator call order, so a numpy major change could alter N_grow (-2); self-test thresholds for the growth lag (0.6 x law) are loose by construction (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py L1539–L1541: Growth-lag acceptance window 0.6 x law <= N_grow <= law + 0.5 is loose <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L1539-L1541>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-repro-package-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sheth et al. (2012) Science distal Hoxa13/Hoxd11-13 + Gli3 dose modulation of Turing digit wavelength on a fan-shaped embryonic autopod, with Pass 3 AER-FGF8 mitogenic outgrowth on a deforming Lagrangian mesh — Source and data traceability: 95/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
