<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sheth et al. (2012) Science distal Hoxa13/Hoxd11-13 + Gli3 dose modulation of Turing digit wavelength on a fan-shaped embryonic autopod, with Pass 3 AER-FGF8 mitogenic outgrowth on a deforming Lagrangian mesh — Morphological realism / specimen match: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The radiograph segmentation (Panels E-F, L820-878) and the inter-digit regularity comparison (Panel H) are unchanged and still visible; the new Panels I-J and the growth-mesh PNG show a narrow early bud widening into a fan with radial digit rays splaying from a quiescent wrist zone, which is closer to the morphology of a developing autopod than the Pass 2 fixed paddles, and the triple-null growing fan carries 13 thin closely spaced rays as in Sheth et al.'s Fig. 1G. Deductions: the WT growing fan shows 3.5 oblique, partly irregular rays rather than 5 straight digits (Panel I; growth lag plus noise-only initiation) (-5); still no side-by-side with Sheth et al.'s own Sox9 in situ panels, only a human radiograph of a different genotype/species (-4); digit rays stop at the sub-Turing wrist gate (L601-603) and never connect to the zeugopod elements (-2); fan edges are straight sector rays, not the rounded AER contour of a real bud (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py L884–L907: _draw_growing_fan: tracer circles/rays and AER rim overlay; the WT panel's 3.5 wavelengths are visibly not pentadactyl <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L884-L907>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

