<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Turing Equal-Diffusion Negative Control (No Digit Patterning for D_u = D_v)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that equal activator and inhibitor diffusivities abolish Turing instability across all spatial wavenumbers, serving as the formal negative control | Variables: tr(J_0) = f_u + g_v: homogeneous Jacobian trace; det(J_0) = f_u g_v - f_v g_u: homogeneous Jacobian determinant; Dq = D k^2: scaled diffusion wavenumber" ;
    dct:source "Sheth et al. (2012) Science 338(6113):1476-1480 Fig. 3 & Suppl. Eqs. (S1)-(S4); Turing (1952) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 237:37-72" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L120-L210>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_015_hox_turing_polydactyly.lean#L19-L41> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def modal_trace_eq_diff (tr_J0 Dq : Int) : Int := tr_J0 - 2 * Dq
def modal_det_eq_diff (det_J0 neg_tr_Dq Dq_sq : Int) : Int :=
  det_J0 + neg_tr_Dq + Dq_sq
theorem sheth_turing_equal_diffusion_no_instability (tr_J0 det_J0 Dq neg_tr_Dq Dq_sq : Int)
    (htr : tr_J0 < 0) (hdet : det_J0 > 0)
    (hDq : Dq ≥ 0) (hterm : neg_tr_Dq ≥ 0) (hsq : Dq_sq ≥ 0) :
    modal_trace_eq_diff tr_J0 Dq < 0 ∧ modal_det_eq_diff det_J0 neg_tr_Dq Dq_sq > 0 := by
  unfold modal_trace_eq_diff modal_det_eq_diff; omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "tr(J_0) < 0 ∧ det(J_0) > 0 ∧ D_u = D_v = D ≥ 1 ⟹ ∀ q = k^2 ≥ 0, tr(J_k) = tr(J_0) - 2 D q < 0 ∧ det(J_k) = det(J_0) - D tr(J_0) q + D^2 q^2 > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.462174>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.32.3.651>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Hox-Modulated Turing Wavelength" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.modal_det_eq_diff" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.sheth_turing_equal_diffusion_no_instability" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Distal Hox/Gli3 Dose Monotonic Wavenumber Scaling & Allelic Series (5 -> 14 Digits)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that progressive genetic removal of distal Hox genes and Gli3 monotonically increases k_c^2(H), shrinking digit stripe wavelength λ(H) and increasing digit number from 5 (WT) -> 7 (Gli3-/-) -> 9 (Hoxd11-13-/-;Gli3-/-) -> 11 -> 14 (triple null) without changing autopod width L | Variables: H ∈ [0, 1]: normalized distal Hoxa13 + Hoxd11-13 gene dose in Gli3-null series; f_u(H): activator self-activation rate; k_c(H): critical Turing wavenumber; N_digits = L / λ(H) = k_c(H)" ;
    dct:source "Sheth et al. (2012) Science 338(6113):1476-1480 Figs. 1-3, pp. 1476-1479" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L215-L335>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_015_hox_turing_polydactyly.lean#L48-L79> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def sheth_trace_J0 (fu : Int) : Int := fu - 200
def sheth_kc_sq (fu : Int) : Int := fu - 2
theorem sheth_hox_dose_monotonic_wavenumber_and_allelic_series (fu1 fu2 : Int)
    (h12 : fu1 < fu2) (h2 : fu2 < 200) :
    sheth_kc_sq fu1 < sheth_kc_sq fu2 ∧
    sheth_trace_J0 fu2 < 0 ∧
    sheth_kc_sq 27 = 5 * 5 ∧
    sheth_kc_sq 51 = 7 * 7 ∧
    sheth_kc_sq 83 = 9 * 9 ∧
    sheth_kc_sq 123 = 11 * 11 ∧
    sheth_kc_sq 198 = 14 * 14 := by
  unfold sheth_kc_sq sheth_trace_J0; omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "k_c^2(H) = (D_v f_u(H) + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v) = f_u(H) - 2 = (14 - 9 H)^2;  H_2 < H_1 ⟹ f_u(H_1) < f_u(H_2) ⟹ k_c^2(H_1) < k_c^2(H_2) ∧ λ(H_2) < λ(H_1)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.462174>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.32.3.651>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Hox-Modulated Turing Wavelength" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.sheth_kc_sq" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.sheth_hox_dose_monotonic_wavenumber_and_allelic_series" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Fan-Shaped Limb Bud Proximodistal Arc Expansion & Distal Digit Mode Selection" ;
    dct:description "Proves why the narrow proximal zeugopod (r=1) supports only 2 skeletal condensations (radius/ulna) while excluding 5-to-14 digit modes, whereas the expanded distal autopod fan (r=3) admits the Hox-tuned digit rays | Variables: r: proximodistal radial coordinate on the fan-shaped limb bud; m: angular digit ray mode number; [k_-^2, k_+^2]: local Turing unstable wavenumber band" ;
    dct:source "Sheth et al. (2012) Science 338(6113):1476-1480 Fig. 3D-F & Fig. 4; Newman & Frisch (1979) Science 205:662-668" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L331-L427>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_015_hox_turing_polydactyly.lean#L86-L107> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def in_fan_autopod_band (k_min_sq k_max_sq m r : Nat) : Bool :=
  decide (k_min_sq * r * r ≤ m * m ∧ m * m ≤ k_max_sq * r * r)
theorem sheth_fan_autopod_proximodistal_mode_selection :
    in_fan_autopod_band 2 4 2 1 = true ∧
    in_fan_autopod_band 2 4 5 1 = false ∧
    in_fan_autopod_band 2 4 9 1 = false ∧
    in_fan_autopod_band 2 4 5 3 = true := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "k_m^2(r) = (m / r)^2 ∈ [k_-^2, k_+^2] ⟺ k_-^2 r^2 ≤ m^2 ≤ k_+^2 r^2" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.462174>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.32.3.651>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Hox-Modulated Turing Wavelength" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.in_fan_autopod_band" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.sheth_fan_autopod_proximodistal_mode_selection" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Digit Number = Autopod Width / Turing Wavelength on an AER-Grown Autopod (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Separates the two control axes of digit number on the growing autopod: AER-driven width (ablation / g_max sweep, Summerbell 1974) and Hox-driven wavelength (Sheth 2012 allelic series); the numerical growing-fan solver reports N_grow against this quasi-static law (slope < 1 = growth-induced wavelength lag) | Variables: L = Θ R(T) · 2500/(2π) um: final distal autopod arc set by AER-FGF8 outgrowth (R(T) from dR/dt = v(R,t)); λ(H) = 2500/k_c(H) um: Hox-tuned Turing wavelength; N: number of digit wavelengths on the rim" ;
    dct:source "Sheth et al. (2012) Science 338(6113):1476-1480 Figs. 2-3; Summerbell (1974) J Embryol Exp Morphol 32:651-660; Kondo & Miura (2010) Science 329:1616-1620" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L457-L755>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_015_hox_turing_polydactyly.lean#L117-L145> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def digit_wavelengths (L lam : Nat) : Nat := L / lam
theorem sheth_growing_autopod_digit_number_law (L1 L2 L lam1 lam2 : Nat)
    (hL : L1 ≤ L2) (hlam : lam1 ≤ lam2) (hpos : 0 < lam1) :
    digit_wavelengths L1 lam1 ≤ digit_wavelengths L2 lam1 ∧
    digit_wavelengths L lam2 ≤ digit_wavelengths L lam1 ∧
    digit_wavelengths 2500 500 = 5 ∧
    digit_wavelengths 2500 357 = 7 ∧
    digit_wavelengths 2500 178 = 14 ∧
    digit_wavelengths 1365 500 = 2 := by
  unfold digit_wavelengths
  exact ⟨Nat.div_le_div_right hL, Nat.div_le_div_left hlam hpos, rfl, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "N(L, λ) = ⌊L / λ⌋;  L_1 ≤ L_2 ⟹ N(L_1, λ) ≤ N(L_2, λ);  0 < λ_1 ≤ λ_2 ⟹ N(L, λ_2) ≤ N(L, λ_1);  N(2500, 500) = 5, N(2500, 357) = 7, N(2500, 178) = 14, N(1365, 500) = 2 (AER ablated at t = 0.6)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.462174>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.32.3.651>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Hox-Modulated Turing Wavelength" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.digit_wavelengths" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.sheth_growing_autopod_digit_number_law" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Growth-Dilution Shift of the Turing Modal Eigenvalue on a Growing Domain (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Formalizes the dilution term of the growing-domain reaction-diffusion equations: digits can condense during AER outgrowth only while σ_max exceeds the rim dilation rate, and AER regression (g → 0) restores the full Turing rate — the mechanism behind the sequential digit emergence kymograph (Panel K) | Variables: g(r,t) = g_max A(t) exp(−(R−r)/l_F): AER-FGF8 kinematic area dilation rate (∇·v = g); σ(k): fixed-domain modal growth rate; σ_g(k): modal growth rate on the growing domain" ;
    dct:source "Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999) Bull Math Biol 61(6):1093-1120; Boehm et al. (2010) PLoS Biol 8(7):e1000420; Sheth et al. (2012) Science 338:1476-1480" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L512-L703>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_015_hox_turing_polydactyly.lean#L148-L174> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def dilution_shifted_eigenvalue (sigma g : Int) : Int := sigma - g
theorem sheth_growth_dilution_turing_threshold (sigma g : Int) :
    (g < sigma → dilution_shifted_eigenvalue sigma g > 0) ∧
    (g ≥ sigma → dilution_shifted_eigenvalue sigma g ≤ 0) ∧
    dilution_shifted_eigenvalue sigma 0 = sigma ∧
    dilution_shifted_eigenvalue 449 195 > 0 ∧
    dilution_shifted_eigenvalue 449 500 < 0 := by
  unfold dilution_shifted_eigenvalue; omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "u_t + v·∇u + (∇·v) u = D∇²u + f(u)  ⟹  J_k → J_k − g I,  σ_g(k) = σ(k) − g;  g < σ ⟹ σ_g > 0;  g ≥ σ ⟹ σ_g ≤ 0;  g = 0 (AER regression) ⟹ σ_g = σ;  449 − 195 > 0 (σ_max = 4.49, g_rim = 1.95)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.462174>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.32.3.651>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Hox-Modulated Turing Wavelength" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.dilution_shifted_eigenvalue" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.sheth_growth_dilution_turing_threshold" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Turing Equal-Diffusion Negative Control (No Digit Patterning for D_u = D_v)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that equal activator and inhibitor diffusivities abolish Turing instability across all spatial wavenumbers, serving as the formal negative control | Variables: tr(J_0) = f_u + g_v: homogeneous Jacobian trace; det(J_0) = f_u g_v - f_v g_u: homogeneous Jacobian determinant; Dq = D k^2: scaled diffusion wavenumber" ;
    dct:source "Sheth et al. (2012) Science 338(6113):1476-1480 Fig. 3 & Suppl. Eqs. (S1)-(S4); Turing (1952) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 237:37-72" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L120-L210>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_015_hox_turing_polydactyly.lean#L19-L41> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def modal_trace_eq_diff (tr_J0 Dq : Int) : Int := tr_J0 - 2 * Dq
def modal_det_eq_diff (det_J0 neg_tr_Dq Dq_sq : Int) : Int :=
  det_J0 + neg_tr_Dq + Dq_sq
theorem sheth_turing_equal_diffusion_no_instability (tr_J0 det_J0 Dq neg_tr_Dq Dq_sq : Int)
    (htr : tr_J0 < 0) (hdet : det_J0 > 0)
    (hDq : Dq ≥ 0) (hterm : neg_tr_Dq ≥ 0) (hsq : Dq_sq ≥ 0) :
    modal_trace_eq_diff tr_J0 Dq < 0 ∧ modal_det_eq_diff det_J0 neg_tr_Dq Dq_sq > 0 := by
  unfold modal_trace_eq_diff modal_det_eq_diff; omega
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "tr(J_0) < 0 ∧ det(J_0) > 0 ∧ D_u = D_v = D ≥ 1 ⟹ ∀ q = k^2 ≥ 0, tr(J_k) = tr(J_0) - 2 D q < 0 ∧ det(J_k) = det(J_0) - D tr(J_0) q + D^2 q^2 > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.462174>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.32.3.651>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Hox-Modulated Turing Wavelength" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.modal_det_eq_diff" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.sheth_turing_equal_diffusion_no_instability" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Distal Hox/Gli3 Dose Monotonic Wavenumber Scaling & Allelic Series (5 -> 14 Digits)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that progressive genetic removal of distal Hox genes and Gli3 monotonically increases k_c^2(H), shrinking digit stripe wavelength λ(H) and increasing digit number from 5 (WT) -> 7 (Gli3-/-) -> 9 (Hoxd11-13-/-;Gli3-/-) -> 11 -> 14 (triple null) without changing autopod width L | Variables: H ∈ [0, 1]: normalized distal Hoxa13 + Hoxd11-13 gene dose in Gli3-null series; f_u(H): activator self-activation rate; k_c(H): critical Turing wavenumber; N_digits = L / λ(H) = k_c(H)" ;
    dct:source "Sheth et al. (2012) Science 338(6113):1476-1480 Figs. 1-3, pp. 1476-1479" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L215-L335>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_015_hox_turing_polydactyly.lean#L48-L79> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def sheth_trace_J0 (fu : Int) : Int := fu - 200
def sheth_kc_sq (fu : Int) : Int := fu - 2
theorem sheth_hox_dose_monotonic_wavenumber_and_allelic_series (fu1 fu2 : Int)
    (h12 : fu1 < fu2) (h2 : fu2 < 200) :
    sheth_kc_sq fu1 < sheth_kc_sq fu2 ∧
    sheth_trace_J0 fu2 < 0 ∧
    sheth_kc_sq 27 = 5 * 5 ∧
    sheth_kc_sq 51 = 7 * 7 ∧
    sheth_kc_sq 83 = 9 * 9 ∧
    sheth_kc_sq 123 = 11 * 11 ∧
    sheth_kc_sq 198 = 14 * 14 := by
  unfold sheth_kc_sq sheth_trace_J0; omega
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "k_c^2(H) = (D_v f_u(H) + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v) = f_u(H) - 2 = (14 - 9 H)^2;  H_2 < H_1 ⟹ f_u(H_1) < f_u(H_2) ⟹ k_c^2(H_1) < k_c^2(H_2) ∧ λ(H_2) < λ(H_1)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.462174>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.32.3.651>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Hox-Modulated Turing Wavelength" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.sheth_kc_sq" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.sheth_hox_dose_monotonic_wavenumber_and_allelic_series" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Fan-Shaped Limb Bud Proximodistal Arc Expansion & Distal Digit Mode Selection" ;
    dct:description "Proves why the narrow proximal zeugopod (r=1) supports only 2 skeletal condensations (radius/ulna) while excluding 5-to-14 digit modes, whereas the expanded distal autopod fan (r=3) admits the Hox-tuned digit rays | Variables: r: proximodistal radial coordinate on the fan-shaped limb bud; m: angular digit ray mode number; [k_-^2, k_+^2]: local Turing unstable wavenumber band" ;
    dct:source "Sheth et al. (2012) Science 338(6113):1476-1480 Fig. 3D-F & Fig. 4; Newman & Frisch (1979) Science 205:662-668" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L331-L427>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_015_hox_turing_polydactyly.lean#L86-L107> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def in_fan_autopod_band (k_min_sq k_max_sq m r : Nat) : Bool :=
  decide (k_min_sq * r * r ≤ m * m ∧ m * m ≤ k_max_sq * r * r)
theorem sheth_fan_autopod_proximodistal_mode_selection :
    in_fan_autopod_band 2 4 2 1 = true ∧
    in_fan_autopod_band 2 4 5 1 = false ∧
    in_fan_autopod_band 2 4 9 1 = false ∧
    in_fan_autopod_band 2 4 5 3 = true := by decide
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "k_m^2(r) = (m / r)^2 ∈ [k_-^2, k_+^2] ⟺ k_-^2 r^2 ≤ m^2 ≤ k_+^2 r^2" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.462174>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.32.3.651>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Hox-Modulated Turing Wavelength" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.in_fan_autopod_band" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.sheth_fan_autopod_proximodistal_mode_selection" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Digit Number = Autopod Width / Turing Wavelength on an AER-Grown Autopod (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Separates the two control axes of digit number on the growing autopod: AER-driven width (ablation / g_max sweep, Summerbell 1974) and Hox-driven wavelength (Sheth 2012 allelic series); the numerical growing-fan solver reports N_grow against this quasi-static law (slope < 1 = growth-induced wavelength lag) | Variables: L = Θ R(T) · 2500/(2π) um: final distal autopod arc set by AER-FGF8 outgrowth (R(T) from dR/dt = v(R,t)); λ(H) = 2500/k_c(H) um: Hox-tuned Turing wavelength; N: number of digit wavelengths on the rim" ;
    dct:source "Sheth et al. (2012) Science 338(6113):1476-1480 Figs. 2-3; Summerbell (1974) J Embryol Exp Morphol 32:651-660; Kondo & Miura (2010) Science 329:1616-1620" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L457-L755>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_015_hox_turing_polydactyly.lean#L117-L145> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def digit_wavelengths (L lam : Nat) : Nat := L / lam
theorem sheth_growing_autopod_digit_number_law (L1 L2 L lam1 lam2 : Nat)
    (hL : L1 ≤ L2) (hlam : lam1 ≤ lam2) (hpos : 0 < lam1) :
    digit_wavelengths L1 lam1 ≤ digit_wavelengths L2 lam1 ∧
    digit_wavelengths L lam2 ≤ digit_wavelengths L lam1 ∧
    digit_wavelengths 2500 500 = 5 ∧
    digit_wavelengths 2500 357 = 7 ∧
    digit_wavelengths 2500 178 = 14 ∧
    digit_wavelengths 1365 500 = 2 := by
  unfold digit_wavelengths
  exact ⟨Nat.div_le_div_right hL, Nat.div_le_div_left hlam hpos, rfl, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "N(L, λ) = ⌊L / λ⌋;  L_1 ≤ L_2 ⟹ N(L_1, λ) ≤ N(L_2, λ);  0 < λ_1 ≤ λ_2 ⟹ N(L, λ_2) ≤ N(L, λ_1);  N(2500, 500) = 5, N(2500, 357) = 7, N(2500, 178) = 14, N(1365, 500) = 2 (AER ablated at t = 0.6)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.462174>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.32.3.651>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Hox-Modulated Turing Wavelength" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.digit_wavelengths" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.sheth_growing_autopod_digit_number_law" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Growth-Dilution Shift of the Turing Modal Eigenvalue on a Growing Domain (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Formalizes the dilution term of the growing-domain reaction-diffusion equations: digits can condense during AER outgrowth only while σ_max exceeds the rim dilation rate, and AER regression (g → 0) restores the full Turing rate — the mechanism behind the sequential digit emergence kymograph (Panel K) | Variables: g(r,t) = g_max A(t) exp(−(R−r)/l_F): AER-FGF8 kinematic area dilation rate (∇·v = g); σ(k): fixed-domain modal growth rate; σ_g(k): modal growth rate on the growing domain" ;
    dct:source "Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999) Bull Math Biol 61(6):1093-1120; Boehm et al. (2010) PLoS Biol 8(7):e1000420; Sheth et al. (2012) Science 338:1476-1480" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L512-L703>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_015_hox_turing_polydactyly.lean#L148-L174> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def dilution_shifted_eigenvalue (sigma g : Int) : Int := sigma - g
theorem sheth_growth_dilution_turing_threshold (sigma g : Int) :
    (g < sigma → dilution_shifted_eigenvalue sigma g > 0) ∧
    (g ≥ sigma → dilution_shifted_eigenvalue sigma g ≤ 0) ∧
    dilution_shifted_eigenvalue sigma 0 = sigma ∧
    dilution_shifted_eigenvalue 449 195 > 0 ∧
    dilution_shifted_eigenvalue 449 500 < 0 := by
  unfold dilution_shifted_eigenvalue; omega
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "u_t + v·∇u + (∇·v) u = D∇²u + f(u)  ⟹  J_k → J_k − g I,  σ_g(k) = σ(k) − g;  g < σ ⟹ σ_g > 0;  g ≥ σ ⟹ σ_g ≤ 0;  g = 0 (AER regression) ⟹ σ_g = σ;  449 − 195 > 0 (σ_max = 4.49, g_rim = 1.95)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.462174>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.32.3.651>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Hox-Modulated Turing Wavelength" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.dilution_shifted_eigenvalue" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_015.sheth_growth_dilution_turing_threshold" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

